1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,643
At two seventeen,

2
00:00:01,763 --> 00:00:03,779
the street should have been empty.

3
00:00:04,511 --> 00:00:07,024
I was only a few turns from home.

4
00:00:08,795 --> 00:00:10,361
Then I saw them.

5
00:00:12,337 --> 00:00:13,221
Two men.

6
00:00:13,341 --> 00:00:15,322
Someone who could not stand.

7
00:00:15,442 --> 00:00:17,430
A car with its engine running.

8
00:00:18,566 --> 00:00:20,721
They lifted him like luggage.

9
00:00:20,841 --> 00:00:22,897
I should have kept driving.

10
00:00:24,249 --> 00:00:25,561
The trunk shut.

11
00:00:25,681 --> 00:00:27,637
Then he looked straight at me.

12
00:00:28,881 --> 00:00:30,160
I hit the gas.

13
00:00:32,513 --> 00:00:34,512
The headlights behind me

14
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:36,019
turned when I did.

15
00:00:37,586 --> 00:00:39,782
Every turn. Every street.

16
00:00:39,902 --> 00:00:40,849
Still there.

17
00:00:42,389 --> 00:00:43,985
One last turn.

18
00:00:44,105 --> 00:00:46,310
The road behind me was empty.

19
00:00:47,655 --> 00:00:49,688
Home. Number seventeen.

20
00:00:51,200 --> 00:00:52,462
My key would not fit.

21
00:00:52,582 --> 00:00:54,784
My hands would not stop shaking.

22
00:00:55,316 --> 00:00:56,779
I locked the door.

23
00:00:56,899 --> 00:00:58,480
Then checked it again.

24
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,132
Upstairs, I moved the curtain.

25
00:01:01,252 --> 00:01:02,795
The black car was waiting.

26
00:01:03,801 --> 00:01:05,347
Then my phone rang.

27
00:01:07,738 --> 00:01:09,306
One million dollars.

28
00:01:09,426 --> 00:01:10,754
All you have to do

29
00:01:10,874 --> 00:01:12,495
is forget what you saw.

30
00:01:14,603 --> 00:01:16,362
Do not call the police.

31
00:01:16,482 --> 00:01:18,810
We know which window you are standing at.

32
00:01:20,692 --> 00:01:23,270
A million dollars. Or the police.

33
00:01:23,390 --> 00:01:24,603
What would you do?
